id: core/projection-and-aperture
title: "Projection, View, expression provision, lens, and aperture"
kind: interface-boundary-contract
status: draft-0.4
updated: 2026-09-01

definitions:
  expression_provision: "a bounded configuration for how selected model material may become available in an interaction: purpose, audience, Arena, aperture, medium, affordances, omissions, portability, allowed Projection kinds, and allowed Move kinds"
  projection: "what an attributed Agent actually expresses, represents, proposes, commits, or attempts into an Arena"
  view: "a purpose-specific rebuildable rendering over canonical IDs and events"
  lens: "a named View rule that foregrounds particular relations"
  aperture: "the scope, depth, time window, and salience included in a View or expression provision"
  orientation_map: "a time-indexed rebuildable View of attributed orientation coverage; never a second canonical state store"
  orientation_inquiry: "a question-facing View that renders one orientation_map lacuna without changing semantic state"
  recursive_cognitive_trace: "a rebuildable View over Question, Position, expression provision, Projection or Move, Consequence, Evaluation, Proof adjudication, Update, and next Question"
  presentation_profile: "scoped and revisable View preferences for wording, order, pacing, density, medium, and accessibility"

known_views:
  - arena
  - timeline
  - proof-and-replay
  - memory
  - causal-graph
  - filesystem
  - world
  - orientation_map
  - orientation_inquiry
  - recursive_cognitive_trace
  - character_view

orientation_presentation_boundary:
  semantic_source: question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
  selection_policy: core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  accepted_preference_contract: schemas/projection-preference.v1.schema.json
  rule: >
    question_key and answer meaning survive a change of wording, order, layout,
    representation_medium, or answer_input_adapter. Inferred presentation fit
    remains a proposal until accepted; measured usefulness is a separate scoped
    claim.

expression_provision_boundary:
  semantic_source: core/source-bound-mental-model.yawn
  draft_contract: schemas/source-bound-yawnbot.v0.1.schema.json
  rules:
    - "Provisioning makes a possible interaction inspectable; it is not the interaction event."
    - "Changing an expression provision does not rewrite the Positions it references."
    - "One Position may enter many provisions without semantic duplication."
    - "A provision may omit or redact material under explicit policy but may not invent an accepted conflicting truth."
    - "Downloadable or connectable packages do not carry identity, private sources, consent, agreement, proof, or effect authority unless separately included and authorized."
    - "An exposure requirement is governance intent, not publication."

character_view_boundary:
  rule: >
    A character may represent one or more semantic records in a memorable,
    playable, or relational View. Appearance, dialogue style, animation, or
    coherent persona does not create Agent identity, persistent memory,
    capability, authority, or principal status.

invariants:
  - "Timeline is a View, not a Yawn kind."
  - "Agent Arena is a View, not canonical state."
  - "Renderer, layout, color, image, character, and navigation state are View concerns unless an Agent expresses them into an Arena."
  - "Expression provision is distinct from Projection."
  - "An Agent Projection remains distinct from its Intention, another Agent's Observation, and the resulting Consequence."
  - "Every Move is a transition-attempting Projection; not every Projection is a Move."
  - "Aperture changes visibility and salience, not truth or permission."
  - "Every interactive rendered object resolves to a stable canonical ID."
  - "Presentation-only events do not alter semantic state."
  - "Color and spatial position never carry semantics alone."
  - "Presentation preference is not a learning-style diagnosis or semantic claim."
  - "A View preference cannot hide safety, authority, privacy, provenance, semantic coverage, Evaluation criteria, or proof."

links:
  - docs/projections/README.md
  - interface/projection-stack.yawn
  - interface/source-bound-yawnbot-workbench-v0.1.yawn
  - interface/yawn-brand-v1.yawn
